# The program of what-is-ruled-out-of-a-layout-that-stays-with-compiled-code-ends-the-process.ir, built to admit the inspector. Every call of `twice` is copied and no compiled code enters it by value: without the flag its entry is closed, and a call from the shell ends the process (ENTERS, in that test).
# With the flag no entry by value is closed. The console takes the object out of the heap as the shell does here (aotFindObjectOfLayout()) and calls the method: it is answered.
# The entry asks for what the body takes for proven. Handed something else by code that is not the program, it throws a TypeError and the process goes on.
# OPTIONS: mechanisms=all admit=Inspector
